L0283: Invalid logical closure or capture

A logical callable must have a logical result and captures that remain meaningful after erasure. It cannot capture an arbitrary live physical value as if it were a logical snapshot. Observe the source through a model first and capture that logical result.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/closure_capture_runtime.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```rust
fn capture(value: u8) -> logic Fn(x: Int) -> Int { |x: Int| x + value }
```

Language, as built: [1.25:2](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.25:2).
